  "criterion": "0.9.3 calibration. Frozen before execution: seed 20261005, 1000 datasets per row.\n\nAll targets are evaluated exactly from the generating Gaussian model (no single\nfuture Bernoulli draws). MCSE is reported for every estimate. Criteria:\nA  Mee beta-expectation interval (beta .80): |mean content - .80| <= .02 + 2 MCSE.\nB  Bias t interval (90%) covers the true mean: coverage >= .90 - 2 SE.\nC  Between-run CV MLS interval (90%) covers the true intermediate SD: coverage >= .90 - 2 SE.\n   Designs for A-C: runs x replicates 6x3 with between/within variance ratio 0, .5, 2;\n   6 runs with 2-3 unequal replicates, ratio .5; 3x3 with ratio 2 (small).\nD  ADA sensitivity upper prediction limit (95%): mean conditional probability that\n   a new run's true sensitivity is at or below the limit >= .95 - .02 - 2 MCSE.\n   6 runs 2-fold dilutions; 6 runs 3-fold; 3 runs 2-fold. Run log-EC50 SD .25,\n   signal noise SD .04 (log), 2 replicates, cut 1.35 on signal/NC.\nE  Two-way (subject x run) bootstrap lower bound, confidence .90, 2000 reps:\n   P(conditional FPR >= target) >= .90 - 2 SE; mean FPR reported. Log-scale\n   Gaussian panels, subject var .09, residual .01, run var 0 or .04:\n   screening .05 with 80 x 6; confirmatory-rate .01 with 300 x 6. A 50-subject\n   screening row checks that the tail-support gate withholds every panel.\nF  Descriptive only: probability that a mid-level QC meets the declared ICH M10\n   point rules (bias 20, CV 20, total error 30) in a 6x3 design, by true bias/CV.\nNo seed, scenario or criterion is changed after running.\n",
